<title>ITALY: Fiat H196 pretax profit 1.547 trln lire.</title>
<headline>Fiat H196 pretax profit 1.547 trln lire.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons pretax profit		    1,547 vs  2,153</p>
<p>Cons pretax profit before</p>
<p>    extraordinary items		   1,538 vs  1,761</p>
<p>    Cons turnover			  40,681 vs 39,070</p>
<p>    Operating profit			1,522 vs  2,017</p>
<p>    Operating margin		    3.7 pct vs  5.2 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Italy's automotive and industrial group Fiat said its operating margin in the second quarter of 1996 was &quot;very close&quot; to 5 percent after an operating margin of 2.5 percent in the first quarter of 1996.  </p>
<p>    Investments			  2,083    vs   1,988</p>
<p>    Research and development	 1,145    vs   1,072</p>
<p>Cash flow (pretax plus depreciation)</p>
<p>					     3,966    vs   4,381</p>
<p>    Net group debt		     2,513    vs   2,486</p>
<p>    Net assets plus minorities    25,872    vs  25,619</p>
<p>    Number of empoyees	     239,330    vs 241,208</p>
<p>    Debt/equity ratio		 10 pct    vs  10 pct</p>
<p>Parent Company results</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 620     vs   312</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
